               <titlePage label="" xml:id="titlePage_b3a6b4b0">
                  <p xml:id="idm25">[emblem consisting of an entrance with the book's title; above 'Gloria musica', an organ below ('magis corde organ') and a lyre] Grundlage | einer | Ehren=Pforte, | woran der | Tüchtigsten Capellmeister, | Componisten, Musikgelehrten, | Tonkünstler &amp;c. | Leben, Wercke, | Verdienste &amp;c. | erscheinen sollen. | Zum fernern Ausbau angegeben | von | Mattheson. | [bottom left column:] HAM- | BURG. | In Verle= | gung [bottom right column:] 1740. | des | Verfassers</p>
               </titlePage>
               <titlePage label="Dedication (sig. [a3v])" xml:id="titlePage_a0097f58">
                  <p xml:id="idm27">dated 'Hamburg, Im August. 1740.'</p>
               </titlePage>
               <titlePage label="Scheibe (p. 310)" xml:id="titlePage_8649e1e2">
                  <p xml:id="idm29">'Scheibe. | * | (<rend xml:id="idm30" fontstyle="italic">ex autogr.</rend>) | Johann Adolph Scheibens, | Marckgräfl. Brandenburg=Culmbachischen Capellmeisters, | Lebens=Lauff, | von ihm selbst entworffen.'</p>
               </titlePage>
               <extent xml:id="extent_ce5cb40c">6 pages </extent>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_444579a6">In 4<rend xml:id="idm33" rend="sup">o</rend>; front flyleaf, title page (sig. [a1r]), blank page with former owner's stamp (sig. [a1v]), dedication (sig. [a2r]), blank page (sig. [a2v]), dedication text (sig. a3r–v), author's foreword (pp. [vii]–xl), index of names (pp. [xli]–xliv), text (pp. [1]–428), index (sigs. Hhh3r–Kkk2v), end flyleaf; in all 488 pages of which Scheibe's autobiography comprises six pages (pp. 310–15).</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
